      "review": {
        "source": "Signed official stable source unchanged; preserve six binary packages, both SONAME 8 libraries, all original symbol guards, installed backends/helpers, public SDK and QCH.",
        "version": "Preserve epoch and upstream version; 4:6.7.5-0supralinux2 supersedes retained failed 4:6.7.5-0supralinux1 and the captured Ubuntu reference; prior assignments remain sealed.",
        "dependencies": "Exact eligible ECM 6.30.0-0supralinux3 and authoritative supplementary Plasma Wayland Protocols 1.22.0-0supralinux1; transport identity, digest and exact CMake metadata require KVM input preflight. Matching Ubuntu Qt/private SDK, Wayland and XCB preserved; XRandR and DPMS dependencies remain enabled. No dependency on KWayland library is invented. Declares hwdata <!nocheck> after observed clean native test failure: Original EDID deviceId assertions require vendor names from /usr/share/hwdata/pnp.ids. Attempt 1 omitted hwdata and failed four EDID rows; seven other KScreen tests and ECM AppStream passed.",
        "tests": "All eight upstream registered CTests enabled and verbose, with built-plugin paths and launcher activation on private reaped D-Bus sessions. Installed public Ubuntu ABI client passes Fake/D-Bus config get/set, EDID, modes, cloning, monitor signals and hotplug, plus actual XRandR discovery and unsupported ScreenDpms properties on owned Xvfb. Same unchanged client after APT upgrade and exact SDK rebuilt consumer; clean baseline before candidate execution. Local Ubuntu preparation passed without a package Attempt. Private installed-client wrappers block the host system bus and discard inherited Qt/QML search paths.",
